    "updated_at": "2016-04-20T13:43:57Z",
    "body": "In this chromium [code review](https://codereview.chromium.org/1901153002/), we are trying to find a way to produce an `<img>` in an fully available state with an intrinsic size of zero. Turns out an svg with 0 width or height never reaches the onload handler.  It is not yet clear whether this change is \"dead spec\".\n",
